                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَاثِيلُ</span></b> 
                        , in the following hemistich of Ibn-Ahmar,
“
                            
                                <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَاثِيلُ قِرْطَاسٍ عَلَى هَبْهَبِيَّةٍ</span>
                            <br />
                        ”
signifies <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُتُبٌ يَكْتُبُونَهَا</span>. (L, in TA, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبِىٌّ</span>,
as signifying a “ light, or active, ” camel.)

